@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@
+# V-653 — three independent platform defects
+
+Three unrelated small fixes, each with a behavior test confirmed red without the fix
+(temporarily stashed just the fix commit's file, ran the new test, restored).
+
+## 1. Precompact timer fired on a killed/archived worker
+
+`AgentSession._schedule_precompact_timer` spawns a bare `asyncio.Task`
+(`app/session.py:727`). `stop()` (server shutdown / manual interrupt) already
+cancelled it via `_cancel_precompact_timer("stop")`, but `SessionManager.remove()`
+(`app/manager.py:1179`, the path `kill_worker` uses) called `session._disconnect_backend()`
+directly and never touched the timer. A worker killed while a timer was pending kept
+its asyncio task alive after the worktree and process were gone; ~25 min later it fired,
+called `compact()` on a session with no backend/worktree, and logged
+`native Codex compact failed: connect failed: FileNotFoundError`
+(examples: nedorosl-lit 28.09 06:13 UTC, tender-scan 27.09 11:04).
+
+Fix: `manager.remove()` calls `session._cancel_precompact_timer("killed")` before
+`_disconnect_backend()`, while the session is still loaded. `remove_scope()` funnels
+through `remove()`, so this also covers scope teardown. Live sessions are unaffected —
+the cancel only touches the in-memory timer task on the object being removed.
+
+Test: `tests/test_manager.py::TestSendAndControl::test_remove_cancels_pending_precompact_timer`
+— spawns a real `_run_precompact_timer` task with a mocked `_fire_precompact_timer`,
+calls `mgr.remove()`, asserts the mock was never invoked after the delay elapses.
+
+## 2. `cron_command` timeout never woke anyone
+
+`_fire_cron_command` (`app/bg_jobs.py`) caught `asyncio.TimeoutError`, wrote
+`[command timed out after 600 seconds]` to `last_output`, and returned — no message
+to the job's target. Root cause of the seedon collector going silent for 4 days.
+
+Fix: on timeout, the target is woken once per streak of consecutive timeouts with a
+message naming the job id, the command, the limit, and what to do; a
+`BgJobManager._cron_command_timeout_notified: set[str]` tracks per-job state
+(mirrors the existing in-memory `_procs`/`_tasks` pattern — no schema change). The
+flag is cleared the moment a run completes without timing out (any exit code, matched
+pattern or not), so the next timeout after a recovery notifies again. Also cleared on
+`cancel()`/`cancel_by_session()` to avoid unbounded growth. `bg_create`'s docstring in
+`app/mcp_stdio.py` updated to describe the new behavior instead of "timeout shows only
+in bg_list".
+
+Test: rewrote `tests/test_bg_jobs.py::TestCronCommand::test_timeout_never_wakes_even_after_partial_match`
+into `test_timeout_notifies_once_then_quiet_until_success` — first timeout wakes and
+checks notice content; second consecutive timeout sends nothing more; a completed
+(non-matching) run clears the flag; the next timeout notifies again
+(`session.send.await_count == 2` at the end).
+
+## 3. V-576 migration (v2→v3) never created `attention_events`
+
+`app/schema.sql` has the table for fresh installs, but `app/startup_migration.py`'s
+v2→v3 step only ever added `tm_tasks.tags` — nothing created `attention_events` for a
+database that reached `schema_version=3` some other way. `notify_user` failed with
+`no such table: attention_events` on VPS and laptop; both were patched by hand with
+the same DDL on 28.09.
+
+Fix: `_ensure_attention_events_table()` runs unconditionally on every `migrate_v576()`
+call (before the `pending_database`/`pending_store` fast-path check), using
+`CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` — a no-op both on freshly-created databases and on the
+two installs where the table was already added by hand. It does not touch
+`user_version` or any other migration bookkeeping, so `migrate_v576()`'s existing
+return shape (`{"state": "already"}` / `{"state": "migrated", ...}`) is unchanged and
+`test_second_start_changes_nothing` still passes untouched.
+
+Test: `tests/test_startup_migration_v576.py::test_missing_attention_events_table_is_created_on_an_already_migrated_database`
+— builds a `schema_version=3` database with the table dropped, runs `migrate_v576`,
+asserts the table exists and the call stays idempotent on a second run.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `.../bin/python -m pytest tests/test_manager.py tests/test_bg_jobs.py tests/test_startup_migration_v576.py -q` — **239 passed, 1 skipped**.
+- `.../bin/python -m pytest tests/test_session.py -q` — **245 passed** (untouched by these changes, run because `manager.py` calls into `session.py`).
+- `.../bin/python -m pytest tests/test_attention_v576.py -q` — **4 passed**.
+- Full suite `.../bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q` run for regressions; see session for result.
+
+CHANGELOG (Unreleased/Fixed) and TODO.md updated for all three items. No Orchestra
+restart performed or requested.
